From e9d67ae28438d9af7dac4714d7a64dbb9475cdb6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 20:36:21 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 27/32] ipa: simple: Support FrameDurationLimits

Video at 60 frames a second needs the application to choose the frame
rate, but the simple pipeline leaves the frame length where the sensor
driver puts it and advertises no frame duration control.

Set the frame length through VBLANK, which the pipeline now writes
through its delayed controls ahead of the exposure:

- FrameDurationLimits, advertised per configured mode from the line
  duration and the VBLANK range, bound the frame length; the AE's
  exposure limit follows the longest frame they allow;
- without limits the frame keeps the driver's default length, as
  before;
- an application's own ExposureTime may lengthen the frame as far as
  the sensor allows, so ExposureTime advertises that range.

The IPA returns the configured mode's controls from configure(), and
the software ISP passes them on as the camera's controls. Report
FrameDuration in metadata.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
